Gallium v3d over a virtio-gpu DRM native context (context type 6,
docs/spec/V3D_NATIVE_CONTEXT.md in nopeekOS).

The loader picks v3d for a virtio_gpu render node whose DRM capset has
context_type 6 (v3d_drm_probe_nctx). The screen then routes its DRM
ioctls through screen->ioctl: natively to the v3d kernel driver, or
through vdrm to the host as ccmds (v3d_virtio.c). Static GET_PARAMs come
from the capset; PERFMON, MULTISYNC_EXT and CPU_QUEUE are reported
unsupported. Submissions run on ring 1 with the guest's syncobjs.

Apply with: patch -p1 against mesa-26.2.7.

